    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "1 kWh is equal to 3.6 × 10⁶ Joules or 1 Commercial Unit of Electricity.",
        "Ammeters are connected in series with ideal zero resistance, while Voltmeters are connected in parallel with ideal infinite resistance.",
        "A fuse wire is always connected in series with the live wire and must have high resistance and a low melting point.",
        "MCBs (Miniature Circuit Breakers) work on the magnetic effect of current, whereas electrical fuses work on the heating effect."
      ],
      "id": "2kg4oli"
